{"step_index":1589,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:58:12Z","thinking":"**Examining Graph Radius Bounds**\n\nInspecting graph theory lemmas relating radius and Roman weight. Focusing on how cardinality constraints influence the radius bound. Considering applying results from `test_merge.lean` to the current challenge. Exploring the connections between adjacency, cardinality, and Roman weight for radius determination.\n\n\n**Analyzing radius inequality bounds**\n\nConsidering the remaining subcase where the graph's radius is greater than 3. Realized that previous reasoning may have missed graphs with radii greater than 3. Attempting to prove `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f` using the available assumptions. This inequality must hold given the problem's constraints.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport itertools\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef bfs_ecc(adj, n, v):\n    dist = {v: 0}\n    q = deque([v])\n    while q:\n        curr = q.popleft()\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\n            if nxt not in dist:\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\n                q.append(nxt)\n    if len(dist) < n:\n        return None\n    return max(dist.values())\n\ndef bfs_dists(adj, n, v):\n    dist = {v: 0}\n    q = deque([v])\n    while q:\n        curr = q.popleft()\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\n            if nxt not in dist:\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\n                q.append(nxt)\n    return dist\n\n# Test all f on paths P_8, P_9, P_10 where rad > 3\nfor n in [8, 9, 10]:\n    adj = {i: [] for i in range(n)}\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        adj[i].append(i + 1)\n        adj[i + 1].append(i)\n    rad = min(bfs_ecc(adj, n, i) for i in range(n))\n    print(f'P_{n}: rad={rad}')\n    for f in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n        W = sum(f)\n        if W >= n: continue\n        valid = True\n        for v in range(n):\n            if f[v] == 0 and not any(f[u] == 2 for u in adj[v]):\n                valid = False; break\n        if not valid: continue\n        c2 = [v for v in range(n) if f[v] == 2]\n        if len(c2) < 2: continue\n        if rad <= 3: continue\n        # rad > 3 and W < n and |V_2| >= 2!\n        # Check if exists v in c2 such that 1 + compl(v, 1) + 1 <= W\n        ok = False\n        for v in c2:\n            d = bfs_dists(adj, n, v)\n            compl = sum(1 for u in range(n) if d[u] > 1)\n            if 1 + compl + 1 <= W:\n                ok = True\n                break\n        if not ok:\n            print(f'P_{n}: W={W}, f={f}, no v in c2 has 1 + compl + 1 <= W!')\n            # Check what k works\n            for k in range(1, rad + 1):\n                for v in range(n):\n                    d = bfs_dists(adj, n, v)\n                    compl = sum(1 for u in range(n) if d[u] > k)\n                    if k + compl + 1 <= W:\n                        # print(f'  worked for v={v}, k={k}')\n                        pass\n            break\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Check if k=1 works when rad > 3","toolSummary":"Test k=1 when rad > 3"}}]}
