g that sum to function values of 0, 1, and 2.\n\n**Establishing a Lower Bound on Sum**\n\nFrom the previous steps, a method of partitioning the vertices by layer and analyzing each layer can be considered. Focus on each layer's contribution to the Roman weight and relate layer cardinalities. The desired lower bound of $\\text{radius } G + 1$ can be proven using the layer decomposition and properties of the Roman dominating function.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/benchmark/challenges_promising13/Challenge_2a2555cc.lean","ContentOffset":0,"EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"View Challenge_2a2555cc.lean","toolSummary":"View Challenge_2a2555cc.lean"}}]}
